{"id":"word:hebrew:H1431","type":"word","title":"גָּדַל","subtitle":"H1431 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to be (causatively make ) large (in various senses, as in body, mind, estate or honor, also in pride)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to גָּדַל (H1431) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 116 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"גָּדַל (gâdal) means to be (causatively make ) large (in various senses, as in body, mind, estate or honor, also in pride) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 17 24."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"גָּדַל","transliteration":"gâdal","pronunciation":"gaw-dal'","strong":"H1431","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1431","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["גָּדְל֣וּ","יִגְדַּ֣ל","הִגְדִּ֖יל","וַ/יִּגְדַּל֙","וַ/יִּגְדַּ֖ל"],"morphs":[["HVhp3ms",14],["HC/Vqw3ms",13],["HVqi3ms",8],["HVqp3cp",6],["HVqp3fs",3],["HC/Vqw3fs",3],["HVpp3ms",3],["HVqp3ms",3],["HC/Vqi3ms",2],["HC/Vpi3ms",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"to be (causatively make ) large (in various senses, as in body, mind, estate or honor, also in pride)","usage":"advance, boast, bring up, exceed, excellent, be(-come, do, give, make, wax), great(-er, come to... estate, things), grow(up), increase, lift up, magnify(-ifical), be much set by, nourish (up), pass, promote, proudly (spoken), tower.","full":"H1431. gadal גָּדַל 115 verb grow up, become great (Aramaic גְּדַל (Ithpe`el), twist, twine , Arabic twist a cord, make firm, strong, become strong , so Late Hebrew) — Qal Perfect ׳ג etc. Gen 38:14 14 t.; suffix גְּדֵלַנִי Job 31:18 ; Imperfect יִגְדַּל etc. Psa 35:27 34t.; — 1 grow up , a. child Gen 21:8 , 20 ; 25:27 ; 38:11 , 14 ; Exod 2:10-11 , (JE) Judg 11:2 ; 13:24 ; Ruth 1:12 ; 1Sam 2:21 ; 3:19 ; 1Kin 12:8 , 10 ( = 2Chr 10:8 , 10 ) 2Kin 4:18 ; כְאָב גְּדֵלַנִי he grew up to me as to a father Job 31:18 ; b. lamb 2Sam 12:3 . 2 become great , a. in extent, wealthy Gen 26:13 (twice in verse); 41:40 (JE) Jer 5:27 ; b. in value . בְּעֵינָ֑י נֶפֶשׁ גָָּֽדְלָה י, ׳בְּעֵינֵי prized by 1Sam 26:24 (twice in verse); c. in intensity, grief Job 2:13 , mourning Zech 12:11 , punishment Lam 4:6 , trespass Ezek 9:6 ; d. in sound, loud cry Gen 19:13 (J); e. in importance, of a king Eccl 2:9 ; 1Kin 10:23 ( = 2Chr 9:22 ) Dan 8:9-10 , (under figure of horn), chief Gen 24:35 ; 48:19 (J), Messiah Micah 5:3 , Jerusalem Ezek 16:7 ; f. of God 2Sam 7:22 ; Psa 104:1 , his works 92:6 , his power Num 14:17 (J). 3 to be magnified , a. house of David Zech 12:7 ; b. Yahweh Psa 35:27 ; 40:17 ; 70:5 ; Mal 1:5 , his name 2Sam 7:26 ( = 1Chr 17:24 ). Pi`el Perfect גִּדַּל Josh 4:14 ; Est 3:1 ; גִּדֵּ֔ל Isa 49:21 ; גִּדֵּ֑לָה 51:18 , etc.; Imperfect יְגַדֵּל 44:14 8 t.; Imperative גַּדְּלוּ Psa 34:4 ; Infinitive גַּדֵּל Num 6:5 3 t.; Participle מְגַדְּלִים 2Kin 10:6 ( מְגַדְּלוֺת Song 5:15 ᵑ7 ᵐ5 Hi Bö De); — 1 cause to grow , e.g. hair Num 6:5 (P), plants Jonah 4:10 ; Isa 44:14 ; Ezek 31:4 ; Song 5:13 ; bring up children 2Kin 10:6 ; Isa 1:2 ; 23:4 ; 49:21 ; 51:18 ; Dan 1:5 ; Hosea 9:12 . 2 make great, powerful Gen 12:2 (J) Josh 3:7 ; 4:14 (D) 1Kin 1:37 , 47 ; 1Chr 29:12 , 25 ; 2Chr 1:1 ; Est 3:1 ; 5:11 ; 10:2 . 3 magnify , a. man Job 7:17 ; b. God Psa 34:4 ; 69:31 . Pu`al Participle plural מְגֻדָּלִים brought up Psa 144:12 . Hiph`il Perfect הִגְדִּיל Psa 41:10 +, etc.; Imperfect יַגְדִּיל Isa 42:21 ; Dan 8:25 , etc.; Infinitive הַגְדִּיל 1Chr 22:8 ; Amos 8:5 ; Participle מַגְדִּיל Psalm 18:51 ( = מִגְדֹּיל in || 2Sam 22:51 ); plural מַגְדִּילִים Psa 35:26 ; &#8212; 1 make great , e.g. shekel Amos 8:5 , pile for fire Ezek 24:9 , joy Isa 9:2 , counsel 28:29 , wisdom Eccl 1:16 , works 2:4 , house of Yahweh 1Chr 22:5 ; the heel Psa 41:10 either lifted high (Ges), or (compare De Now) gave me insidiously a great fall ; compare ׳ג מִּיךָ Obadiah 12 i.e. utter proud words (see רחב Hiph`il) 2 magnify , salvation Psalm 18:51, so || 2Sam 22:51 (Kt מַגְדִּיל ; &gt; Qr מִגְדֹּל ), mercy Gen 19:19 (J), teaching Isa 42:21 , the word of Yahweh Psa 138:2 . 3 do great things לַעֲשׂוֺת הִגְדִּיל , a. in a good sense , of God Psa 126:2 ; 126:3 ; Joel 2:21 , also pregnant without Infinitive 1Sam 12:24 . b. in bad sense , of 'the northern one' Joel 2:20 , also pregnant without Infinitive Lam 1:9 ; Zeph 2:8 , 10 ; Dan 8:4 , 8 , 11 , 25 ; with עַל , of enemies Psa 35:26 ; 38:17 ; 55:13 ; Job 19:5 ; Jer 48:26 , 42 ; Ezek 35:13 of speaking ׳ג בְּפִיכֶם עָלַי . c. also, with Infinitive implied, wept greatly 1Sam 20:41 . Hithpa`el Perfect וְהִתְגַּדִּלְתִּ֫י Ezek 38:23 I will magnify myself , shew myself great and powerful (of God); Imperfect יִתְגַּדֵּל , with עַל in a bad sense, magnify oneself against Isa 10:15 ; Dan 11:36 ; יִתְגַּדָּ֑ל 11:37 .","rootNote":"a primitive root; properly, to twist (compare 1434 ), i.e.","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 17 24","keyReferences":["1Chr 17 24","1Chr 22 5","1Chr 29 12","1Chr 29 25","1Kgs 1 37","1Kgs 1 47","1Kgs 10 23","1Kgs 12 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":116,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 17 24","book":"1Chr","chapter":17,"verse":24,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/יִגְדַּ֨ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqi3ms"},{"reference":"1Chr 22 5","book":"1Chr","chapter":22,"verse":5,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/הַגְדִּ֨יל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vhc"},{"reference":"1Chr 29 12","book":"1Chr","chapter":29,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/גַדֵּ֥ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Vpc"},{"reference":"1Chr 29 25","book":"1Chr","chapter":29,"verse":25,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַ/יְגַדֵּ֨ל","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpw3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 37","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":37,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וִֽ/יגַדֵּל֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vpi3ms"},{"reference":"1Kgs 1 47","book":"1Kgs","chapter":1,"verse":47,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"